Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:14:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] The deepening's API, gate 96's repairs: noEdge_iff, the
 window step harvested, the head-form walk equation, attribution
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- NoEdge lands with noEdge_iff (finding 1).
- CfgRecord's private recordStep_window is public as Cfg.InWindow.apply_iff,
  over any alphabet, beside Cfg.InWindow.mono; apply_of_lt follows from the
  two, and the record step cites apply_iff (finding 2).
- PathWalk gains walkLe_succ_iff_head (decision 4's fourth equation);
  Reach's chain_of_walkLe reads walks at the front and Reach imports
  PathWalk instead of ISCountMath (finding 3).
- The four oracle and window-run equations state their formulas; Radius's
  module list names its equations (finding 4).
- The deepening cites [Sip13, §8.1, proof of Thm 8.5]; the AB09 tags read
  as cf. (finding 5). mem_iff_reach_of_noEdge's docstring adds that no
  configuration-count bound is assumed (note 7).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
